@startuml bit-transfer
' Bit transfer (docs/spec/01-physical-layer.md, section 1.3). One clock period = 20 time units.
' DATA low = 1, released (high) = 0. Changes only while CLK is low; sampled on the rising edge (marked).
scale 10 as 90 pixels
hide time-axis
binary "CLK" as CLK
binary "DATA" as DATA
concise "Bit" as BIT

@0
CLK is low
DATA is high
BIT is {-}
@3
DATA is low
BIT is "1"
@10
CLK is high
@20
CLK is low
@23
DATA is high
BIT is "0"
@30
CLK is high
@40
CLK is low
@43
DATA is low
BIT is "1"
@50
CLK is high
@60
CLK is low
@63
BIT is "1"
@70
CLK is high
@80
CLK is low
@83
DATA is high
BIT is "0"
@90
CLK is high
@100
CLK is low
@103
BIT is {-}

highlight 10 to 11 #Gold : sample
highlight 30 to 31 #Gold : sample
highlight 50 to 51 #Gold : sample
highlight 70 to 71 #Gold : sample
highlight 90 to 91 #Gold : sample

CLK@40 <-> @60 : T_CLK
DATA@20 <-> @30 : T_CLK_LOW
@enduml
